;; repr/haskell's corpus (doc/haskell/SPEC.md §9.4, HS4): GHC 9.14.1's boot libraries from its source
;; distribution, fetched once into .tmp/repr-haskell/corpus/ and checked by its hash
;; (bin/repr-haskell corpus fetch), each package converted under its own configuration (SPEC
;; §2.7). Read with the Clojure reader. A package's :modules are the modules the host's GHC
;; installed for it (ghc-pkg field PKG exposed-modules,hidden-modules: the .cabal.in's modules
;; for this OS, flags and bignum backend, without re-exports), each with its source under :dir;
;; :hsc and :boot list the modules R6 converts (hsc2hs, boot files), not R1 (SPEC §10.1);
;; :generated the modules without a source in the tarball (genprimopcode's output).
;; R6 (doc/haskell/HASKELL-NOTES.md, "R6"): a package's :hsc modules are converted from hsc2hs's
;; output (run by the helper with the package's :hsc-flags, as the interface level runs it, the
;; output X.hs beside X.hsc), its :boot files as boot files, and the literate modules of
;; libraries/, the Setup scripts of four packages, are four entries PKG-Setup at the end: Main
;; modules, parsed and compiled as cabal-install compiles a package's Setup script (ghc --make
;; Setup.lhs against the installed Cabal, GHC's default language).
;; :ghc-flags are the flags the helper parses with (after the language and extensions): the
;; package's -this-unit-id, its dependencies' include directories for CPP, its cpp-options and
;; include-dirs (SPEC §2.8). $libdir is `ghc --print-libdir`, $repo the checkout.
;; R5 (doc/haskell/HASKELL-NOTES.md, "R5"): the other 37 packages of the tarball's libraries/ that
;; the host's GHC installs, in dependency order; each package's configuration is its .cabal
;; library's as Cabal configures it for this platform (test/haskell/cabal-info/CabalInfo.hs, with
;; hadrian's :cabal-flags): :language (Haskell98 when the .cabal names none, as Cabal),
;; :extensions (default-extensions), its cpp-options and include-dirs in :ghc-flags, with
;; -package for each build-depends (the installed packages: every package compiles against the
;; host's, R2's way) and the macros of Cabal's cabal_macros.h a module needs (Cabal's
;; CURRENT_PACKAGE_KEY, ghc-heap's MIN_TOOL_VERSION_ghc). :extract a directory to extract instead
;; of :dir (the tarball hard-links containers' files from containers-tests); :configure the
;; headers the package's configure script makes (Cabal's build-type Configure), run once in the
;; extracted tree; :generated-files the generated modules' sources, committed in
;; test/haskell/generated/ (as hadrian and Cabal generate them); :hsc-flags with Cabal's macros
;; for hsc2hs (test/haskell/generated/ghc-9.14.1/cabal_macros.h).
{:tarball {:url "https://downloads.haskell.org/ghc/9.14.1/ghc-9.14.1-src.tar.xz"
           :size 33970212
           :sha256 "2a83779c9af86554a3289f2787a38d6aa83d00d136aa9f920361dd693c101e77"
           :root "ghc-9.14.1"}
 :ghc "9.14.1"
 ;; The interface level (SPEC §9.3, milestone R2; bin/repr-haskell roundtrip --iface): each
 ;; package's modules compiled by ghc --make with its :ghc-flags (the parse's, -haddock among
 ;; them) and :opt, once from the originals and once with the printed modules in their places;
 ;; the modules R1 does not convert (:hsc through hsc2hs with :hsc-flags, :generated by
 ;; genprimopcode, :boot as they are) are the same on both sides. :extract names what the level
 ;; needs of the tarball besides the packages: genprimopcode, built by the host's GHC with
 ;; :packages, and primops.txt.pp, preprocessed by :cpp (as hadrian's HsCpp, SPEC §8.5).
 :iface {:opt ["-O1"]
         :extract ["utils/genprimopcode" "compiler/GHC/Builtin/primops.txt.pp"]
         :genprimopcode {:dir "utils/genprimopcode" :main "Main.hs" :packages ["containers" "array"]
                         :primops "compiler/GHC/Builtin/primops.txt.pp"
                         :cpp ["cc" "-E" "-undef" "-traditional" "-P" "-x" "c"]}}
 :packages
